    "result_text": "A held claim now counts in claimed again. Its amount is included in the person's claimed figure, the claimed-total, and the `claimed=` / `claimed-total=` fields of the ROLLUP and TOTALS audit lines. While it's held, only its due figures stay out of the totals. This applies to both kinds of hold, a person's and a claim's. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**Server (`Rollup.java`):** I added a check, `claims(...)`, that decides whether a claim counts toward claimed. It still requires a counting status and leaves out claims deferred past the sheet's today, but it ignores holds. The existing `counts(...)` check, which does leave held claims out, now only decides whether the claim's due is added. I updated the class comment to match.\n\n**Front end:** The claimed figures (`person-claimed`, `rollup-claimed-total`) no longer look at holds. I added a `useRetiredHolds` hook in `people.slot.tsx` so they still leave out a retired person's open claims. `useHeld` and everything that sums due figures are unchanged.\n\n**Decision for you:** retirement still takes a person's open claims out of claimed. The request only mentions holds, but the code treats retirement the same way, so I left retirement alone. The tests pass either way. If retirement should also stop affecting claimed, it's a one-line change in each of `claims(...)` and `sumAmounts`.\n\nI made one comment-only edit in `useClaims.ts` after the passing run and didn't re-run the tests for it.",
